{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && git status --short && printf '\\\\n-- packet --\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' lean/finite_fibers/aristotle_tasks/FF20-stabilizer-support-corner-instantiation.md && printf '\\\\n-- likely handoff/status --\\\\n' && rg -n -i \\\"FF20|aristotle|handoff|status\\\" AGENTS.md README.md PROGRESS.md HANDOFF.md . 2>/dev/null | head -160\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n M ../AGENTS.md\n M ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/README.md\n D ../writing/.type_II_stabilizer_proof.tex.swp\n D ../writing/prl_stabilizer_region_algebras/.main.tex.swp\n?? ../.gitignore\n?? ../AristotleCandidates/\n?? ./\n?? ../project_graph.json\n?? ../project_graph.schema.json\n?? ../research/\n?? ../sources/Nielsen_Chuang.pdf\n?? ../sources/Rudin.pdf\n?? ../sources/Wilde_book.pdf\n?? ../sources/absorbtion_D3_brane.pdf\n?? ../sources/quantum-computation-and-quantum-information-nielsen-chuang.pdf\n?? ../sources/thermodynamic_irreversibility.pdf\n?? ../support_corner_stabilizer.pdf\n?? ../support_corner_stabilizer.tex\n?? ../validate_project_graph.py\n?? ../work/2026-07-topological-order-invariants/\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/PROOF-HANDOFF.md\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I002-general-stabilizer-criterion/\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I003-half-chain-finite-support-obstruction/\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I004-ogata-surface-code-cone-algebras/\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I005-flat-stabilizer-support-corners-and-sector-classification/\n?? ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/\n?? ../work/AGENTS.md\n?? ../work/aristotle_autopilot/\n?? ../work/overleaf_publication_audit/\n?? ../writing/canonical_stabilizer_appendix_blueprint/\n?? ../writing/prl_stabilizer_region_algebras_canonical_appendix_draft/\n\n-- packet --\n# FF20 — instantiate the support-corner theorem from an actual stabilizer model\n\nRead the full manuscript source and work only in `formalization_finite_fibers`.\n\nCreate only `FiniteFiber/ActualStabilizerSupportCorner.lean`. Combine the\nactual finite full-Pauli local system of FF18 and the C-star/GNS interface of\nFF19 with the already checked `StabilizerFiniteFiber` theorem. State a\nconditional theorem whose hypotheses are exactly the remaining global facts:\nthe completed state/GNS representation, decreasing finite stabilizer supports,\ntheir strong limit, dense orbit/fullness, and corner traciality. Its conclusion\nmust be the existing every-nonzero-central-summand finite-projection statement.\n\nDo not claim those global hypotheses follow from the current manuscript's\nshort-range definition unless they have actually been constructed. Do not state\na direct-integral/type-III classification theorem. No axioms/placeholders.\n\nAcceptance: `lake build FiniteFiber.ActualStabilizerSupportCorner` succeeds,\nand the result is labelled conditional unless every listed global input is\nproved in the submitted snapshot.\n\n-- likely handoff/status --\nHANDOFF.md:1:# Handoff: finite-fiber support-corner formalization\nHANDOFF.md:160:## I004 countable-representation status\nHANDOFF.md:177:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/HANDOFF.md`.\nHANDOFF.md:181:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF05-FF07-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\nHANDOFF.md:185:stale HANDOFF deletion, and metadata were rejected.  The review is at\nHANDOFF.md:186:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF08-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\nHANDOFF.md:198:remote snapshot remains quarantined under `aristotle_responses/FF10-extracted/`.\nHANDOFF.md:206:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF10-finite-region-qubit-local-algebras.md`\nHANDOFF.md:207:and `aristotle_responses/FF10-prompt-adversarial-review.md`; the post-result\nHANDOFF.md:208:review is `aristotle_responses/FF10-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\nHANDOFF.md:215:`aristotle_responses/FF11-extracted/`.  Only\nHANDOFF.md:216:`AristotleCandidates/FiniteRegionPauliMatrices.lean` was integrated; it is\nHANDOFF.md:218:stale deletion of the FF11 handoff status, `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md`, and its\nHANDOFF.md:230:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF11-finite-region-pauli-matrices.md`,\nHANDOFF.md:231:`aristotle_responses/FF11-prompt-adversarial-review.md`, and\nHANDOFF.md:232:`aristotle_responses/FF11-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\nHANDOFF.md:239:`aristotle_responses/FF12-extracted/`.  Only\nHANDOFF.md:240:`AristotleCandidates/OneSitePauliNormalForm.lean` was integrated; it is\nHANDOFF.md:243:remote README attribution insertion, stale removal of the live FF12 status\nHANDOFF.md:244:from the handoff, and `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` were rejected.\nHANDOFF.md:255:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF12-one-site-pauli-normal-form.md`,\nHANDOFF.md:256:`aristotle_responses/FF12-prompt-adversarial-review.md`, and\nHANDOFF.md:257:`aristotle_responses/FF12-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\nHANDOFF.md:294:## Status discipline\nHANDOFF.md:383:Aristotle archive metadata claiming commit/push was not integrated.\nHANDOFF.md:419:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF15-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\nREADME.md:14:Read [HANDOFF.md](HANDOFF.md) before editing.  In particular, distinguish:\n./HANDOFF.md:1:# Handoff: finite-fiber support-corner formalization\n./HANDOFF.md:160:## I004 countable-representation status\n./HANDOFF.md:177:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/HANDOFF.md`.\n./HANDOFF.md:181:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF05-FF07-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n./HANDOFF.md:185:stale HANDOFF deletion, and metadata were rejected.  The review is at\n./HANDOFF.md:186:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF08-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n./HANDOFF.md:198:remote snapshot remains quarantined under `aristotle_responses/FF10-extracted/`.\n./HANDOFF.md:206:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF10-finite-region-qubit-local-algebras.md`\n./HANDOFF.md:207:and `aristotle_responses/FF10-prompt-adversarial-review.md`; the post-result\n./HANDOFF.md:208:review is `aristotle_responses/FF10-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n./HANDOFF.md:215:`aristotle_responses/FF11-extracted/`.  Only\n./HANDOFF.md:216:`AristotleCandidates/FiniteRegionPauliMatrices.lean` was integrated; it is\n./HANDOFF.md:218:stale deletion of the FF11 handoff status, `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md`, and its\n./HANDOFF.md:230:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF11-finite-region-pauli-matrices.md`,\n./HANDOFF.md:231:`aristotle_responses/FF11-prompt-adversarial-review.md`, and\n./HANDOFF.md:232:`aristotle_responses/FF11-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n./HANDOFF.md:239:`aristotle_responses/FF12-extracted/`.  Only\n./HANDOFF.md:240:`AristotleCandidates/OneSitePauliNormalForm.lean` was integrated; it is\n./HANDOFF.md:243:remote README attribution insertion, stale removal of the live FF12 status\n./HANDOFF.md:244:from the handoff, and `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` were rejected.\n./HANDOFF.md:255:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF12-one-site-pauli-normal-form.md`,\n./HANDOFF.md:256:`aristotle_responses/FF12-prompt-adversarial-review.md`, and\n./HANDOFF.md:257:`aristotle_responses/FF12-integration-adversarial-review.md`.\n./HANDOFF.md:294:## Status discipline\n./HANDOFF.md:383:Aristotle archive metadata claiming commit/push was not integrated.\n./HANDOFF.md:419:`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF15-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n./README.md:14:Read [HANDOFF.md](HANDOFF.md) before editing.  In particular, distinguish:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
