model rather than assumed.\n\nThe main result, `actualStabilizerSystem_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit`, is explicitly **conditional**. Its hypotheses are exactly the remaining global facts: (1) a quasilocal C*-completion of the local algebras; (2) a global stabilizer state extending the compatible finite local states, with its GNS data; (3) a von Neumann algebra on the GNS space containing the represented finite local algebras; (4) an increasing sequence of finite stabilizer subgroups, giving the decreasing finite stabilizer supports; (5) strong convergence of those supports to `q` (dropped in the canonical-limit variant, which uses the constructed strong limit); (6) the GNS-orbit data — regional commutation, dense product orbit/fullness, and corner traciality. Its conclusion is the existing `SupportCornerConclusion`, whose `central_witness` field is the manuscript's every-nonzero-central-summand finite-projection statement; this is restated separately as `actualStabilizerSystem_central_witness_of_gnsOrbit`, with `actualStabilizerSystem_semifinite_of_gnsOrbit` as the semifiniteness corollary.\n\nNo claim is made that hypotheses (1)–(6) follow from the manuscript's short-range definition — none of them is constructed here — and no direct-integral or type-III classification statement is stated. The module docstring enumerates exactly what is constructed versus assumed, and `HANDOFF.md` records a matching closeout entry. All work is committed and pushed.-- prohibited tokens candidate --\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
